🚀  Day 11 of #90DaysOfDevOps

✔️ Today i worked on linux file ownership & group management concepts:

✔️ Understanding filr ownership & groups

✔️ Using chown to change file owners

✔️ Using chgrp to change groups

✔️ Managing owner & group together

✔️ Recursive ownership change with chown -R

✔️ Creating users & group in linux 

✔️ Verifying permission using -l


Below commands i used :

ls -l : long file listing

touch : create empty file

mkdir : create empty dirctory

mkdir -p : create a nested directories

useradd : create user

groupadd : create group

chown : change owner

chown:group : change both

chown -R : recursive ownership 

ls -lR : recursive listing


Learning linux administration step by step building strong DevOps fundamentals. 🔥 

